,"rationale":"The bill creates new federal civil causes of action and judicial review procedures, which would generate litigation between pharmacists and PBMs."}],"plainSummary":"This bill would allow pharmacists to sue pharmacy benefit managers (PBMs) in federal court if they believe PBM fees or contract terms are unfair, and would let courts review and potentially overturn those fees. The bill applies specifically to prescription drug plans offered to federal employees and retirees. It creates a new legal pathway for pharmacists to challenge the business practices of the middlemen who manage drug benefits.","classificationMethod":"llm","plain":{"whoItTouches":"Anyone who fills a prescription. Anyone who pays a medical bill.","confidence":"title-only"},"topOverlap":{"bioguideId":"H001086","score":0.05366184557252676},"overlapCount":40},"meaning":{"percentile":84.00378608613346,"median":0.01073720309570498,"n":6339,"ordinary":[],"unattributedShare":0.418992356286287}},{"billId":"119-hr-2902","bioguideId":"F000481","cycle":2026,"score":0.01974571029458446,"matches":[{"industry":"insurance","donorAmount":34000,"donorShare":0.03770976402837881,"billConfidence":0.6,"contribution":0.009628024858309483},{"industry":"health-providers","donorAmount":21250,"donorShare":0.02356860251773676,"billConfidence":0.85,"contribution":0.00852481367662819},{"industry":"pharma","donorAmount":3750,"donorShare":0.00415916515018884,"billConfidence":0.9,"contribution":0.0015928717596467897}],"method":{"formula":"score = Σ_industries ( donorShare(industry) × billWeight(industry) ), where billWeight = classifierConfidence / Σ classifierConfidence. Range 0–1, read as a weighted share of disclosed itemized money.","donorProfileCycle":2026,"billClassificationMethod":"llm","unclassifiedDonorShare":0.418992356286287},"bill":{"id":"119-hr-2902","congress":119,"billType":"hr","billNumber":"2902","title":"SOAR Act of 2025","introducedDate":"2025-04-10","latestActionDate":"2025-04-10","latestActionTex