l-estate","confidence":0.7,"rationale":"Statehood would change property tax authority and land-use regulation for most of the current District, affecting developers and property owners."},{"industry":"legal","confidence":0.6,"rationale":"The transition of DC courts, judicial proceedings, and contractual obligations to state authority would affect legal practice and litigation in the new jurisdiction."}],"plainSummary":"This bill would admit most of the current District of Columbia as the 51st state, called Washington, Douglass Commonwealth, with two senators and one representative in Congress. A small federal district containing the Capitol, White House, Supreme Court, and nearby monuments would remain as the seat of the federal government. The bill sets up a transition process for DC laws, courts, contracts, and obligations to continue under state authority, and creates a commission to manage the shift to statehood.","classificationMethod":"llm","plain":{"whoItTouches":"Anyone who votes.","confidence":"crs-summary"},"topOverlap":{"bioguideId":"M001245","score":0.050448841212731466},"overlapCount":197},"meaning":{"percentile":66.08297838775832,"median":0.01073720309570498,"n":6339,"ordinary":[],"unattributedShare":0.418992356286287}},{"billId":"119-hr-8791","bioguideId":"F000481","cycle":2026,"score":0.014529350257993014,"matches":[{"industry":"education","donorAmount":13100,"donorShare":0.014529350257993014,"billConfidence":0.85,"contribution":0.014529350257993014}],"method":{"formula":"score = Σ_industries ( donorShare(industry) × billWeight(industry) ), where billWeight = classifierConfidence / Σ classifierConfidence. Range 0–1, read as a weighted share of disclosed itemized money.","donorProfileCycle":2026,"billClassificationMethod":"keyword-fallback","unclassifiedDonorShare":0.418992356286287},"bill":{"id":"119-hr-8791","congress":119,"billType":"hr","billNumber":"8791","title":"IGNITE HBCU Excellence Act","introducedDate":"2026-05-13","latestActionDate":"2026-